    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p3-p2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x^3-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x-1)(x^2+x+1)$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^3-1&=x^3-1^3\\\\x^3-1&=(x-1)(x^2+x+1).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 13
      },
      {
        "id": "p3-p2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$27x^3-8$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(3x-2)(9x^2+6x+4)$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}27x^3-8&=(3x)^3-2^3\\\\27x^3-8&=(3x-2)\\bigl((3x)^2+(3x)(2)+2^2\\bigr)\\\\27x^3-8&=(3x-2)(9x^2+6x+4).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 17
      },
      {
        "id": "p3-p2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$(2x+1)^3-8$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(2x-1)(4x^2+8x+7)$",
          "worked": "Let $u=2x+1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}u^3-8&=u^3-2^3\\\\u^3-8&=(u-2)(u^2+2u+4).\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe linear factor is $u-2=2x-1$. The quadratic factor simplifies as follows.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}u^2+2u+4&=(2x+1)^2+2(2x+1)+4\\\\u^2+2u+4&=4x^2+4x+1+4x+2+4\\\\u^2+2u+4&=4x^2+8x+7.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $(2x+1)^3-8=(2x-1)(4x^2+8x+7)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      }
    ]
  },
